wardenname=The Sky Warden
wardenintro1=Hm. Stairs. Nobody has taken the stairs in a long, long while.
wardenintro2=I am the Warden. The last one, if you keep count. I keep the light. Kept, rather. It went out with the storm.
wardenintro3=Take this windsilk. You climbed all this way; it would be rude to send you off with empty pockets.
wardenrecruit1=Here is a strange thing to ask a stranger: my order kept the sky for four hundred years, and I am the last name on its roster. A keeper without a tower is just an old man in the wind.
wardenrecruit2=Hire me. One hundred thousand coins - the Skywatch pension was generous, and I intend to spend it working. Build me a tower of my own down there, give me a bed, and I will keep YOUR light instead.
wardenrecruitwait=A hundred thousand, friend. Coin first - then you get the oldest sky-sailor in the Reach as a neighbour.
wardenrecruitdone1=Ha! Paid in full. Then it is settled: the Skywatch serves a new house now. Yours.
wardenrecruitdone2=I will take the long way down and wait by your stairway. Go on home, build me something with a view - and we will see what else is still worth finding up here.
wardenrecruitnohome=You climbed into my sky without leaving a stairway behind you? Go home, set your front door in order - then we will talk about me moving.
wardengivesbell=One more thing. Take the old bell - it opens doors that are not doors. You will know when.
wardensettlertip=Recruited above the clouds, for a fortune in coin.
wardenfarewell=The tower is quiet now. My new post suits me better.
gatenobinding=The gate hums, dormant. It has nowhere to take you yet - ascend from your own stairway first.
wardenshopclosed=My shelves are dark, like everything else here. Light the beacon first.
wardencatfound1=Mrrp?
wardencattreat=The cat snatches the treat and vanishes in a puff of cloud - homeward.
wardencatnotreat=The cat eyes you warily. It clearly expects a snack.

